  "/privacy": {
    "routePath": "/privacy",
    "pageKind": "privacy",
    "title": "Privacy Policy · CodeExplorer",
    "description": "CodeExplorer is a 100% local, privacy-first developer tool. Zero telemetry, zero cloud dependencies, zero source code transmission.",
    "canonical": "https://code-explorer.app/privacy",
    "ogUrl": "https://code-explorer.app/privacy",
    "ogTitle": "Privacy Policy · CodeExplorer",
    "ogDescription": "CodeExplorer is a 100% local, privacy-first developer tool. Zero telemetry, zero cloud dependencies, zero source code transmission.",
    "mainHtml": "<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>\r\n      <div class=\"meta\">Effective Date: October 29, 2026 · Standalone Open Source Software</div>\r\n\r\n      <div class=\"card\">\r\n        <h2>1. Summary &amp; Core Principles</h2>\r\n        <p>\r\n          CodeExplorer (CLI binary <code>ce</code> and the VS Code Extension <code>code-explorer-vscode</code>) is designed from the ground up as a <strong>100% local-first, privacy-by-design</strong> architecture intelligence engine.\r\n        </p>\r\n        <ul>\r\n          <li><strong>Zero Telemetry:</strong> CodeExplorer does not collect, record, or transmit usage statistics, crash dumps, or telemetry.</li>\r\n          <li><strong>Zero Code Transmission:</strong> Your source code, AST, tokens, git history, and architecture graphs never leave your local machine or your CI/CD runner.</li>\r\n          <li><strong>Local Database:</strong> All parsed architecture data is stored in a local SQLite database (<code>.codeexplorer/codeexplorer.db</code>) within your project repository.</li>\r\n          <li><strong>No User Accounts:</strong> We do not require registration, accounts, or authentication to use CodeExplorer.</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n      <div class=\"card\">\r\n        <h2>2. Website (code-explorer.app)</h2>\r\n        <p>\r\n          The website <code>code-explorer.app</code> is a static documentation and download portal hosted on an isolated server.\r\n        </p>\r\n        <p>\r\n          Standard web server access logs (client IP address, user-agent, requested URL, and timestamp) are processed strictly for operational security, DDOS mitigation, and anonymous aggregate visitor counts. No advertising cookies, third-party trackers, or personal tracking scripts are loaded on this website.\r\n        </p>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n      <div class=\"card\">\r\n        <h2>3. Local Architecture Engine Execution</h2>\r\n        <p>\r\n          When you execute <code>ce scan</code>, <code>ce map</code>, or <code>ce gate</code>, or when you interact with the VS Code extension or MCP server:\r\n        </p>\r\n        <ul>\r\n          <li>The analysis executes exclusively on your CPU using local Roslyn/Tree-sitter parsers.</li>\r\n          <li>No external network requests are made during scanning or invariant checking.</li>\r\n          <li>MCP agent interactions (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot) are mediated locally via standard input/output (stdio) with your local client.</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n      <div class=\"card\">\r\n        <h2>4. Open Source Transparency &amp; License</h2>\r\n        <p>\r\n          CodeExplorer is free and open-source software released under the <a href=\"https://github.com/vmikhailov/code-explorer/blob/main/LICENSE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: var(--accent);\">MIT License</a>. The entire source code is publicly inspectable and auditable on <a href=\"https://github.com/vmikhailov/code-explorer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: var(--accent);\">GitHub</a>.\r\n        </p>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n      <div class=\"card\">\r\n        <h2>5. Contact</h2>\r\n        <p>\r\n          If you have questions regarding this privacy policy or security practices, you can open an issue on the official GitHub repository at <a href=\"https://github.com/vmikhailov/code-explorer/issues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: var(--accent);\">github.com/vmikhailov/code-explorer/issues</a>.\r\n        </p>\r\n      </div>"
  }
